# HTTP-header-level CSP hardening on top of the meta-tag CSP in
# index.html/play.html — see README.md. `frame-ancestors` and
# `X-Frame-Options` can only be set via HTTP headers, never a <meta> tag,
# so they live here instead. This file uses the Netlify/Cloudflare Pages
# `_headers` convention (copied verbatim from public/ into dist/ by Vite);
# other static hosts need the equivalent config in their own format.

/play.html
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# play.html runs inside an iframe sandboxed *without* `allow-same-origin`
# (see README.md), so it has a unique opaque origin on every load — every
# subresource fetch it makes (its own JS/CSS bundle, wasmoon's glue.wasm,
# content images) is therefore cross-origin *with respect to this same
# server*, even though the URL is same-path. Vite already marks the module
# script/stylesheet tags `crossorigin`, so the browser sends those as real
# CORS requests; without this header those requests — and everything else
# play.html fetches — would be blocked, and the game would fail to load
# entirely. This is intentionally wide open (`*`): nothing served here is
# per-user or credentialed, and the isolation this app relies on comes from
# the opaque origin/CSP, not from withholding CORS.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
